{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/47110-gmc-virtue-vice","id":47110,"title":"GMC Virtue/Vice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-11T15:50:46-08:00","id":47110,"title":"GMC Virtue/Vice","content":"Sorry if this has been said before.<br /> <br /> My idea is that Prometheans could have a Nature and a Aspiration (trying to come up with another name for the latter).<br /> The first one is how he is while the second is a trait in humanity he admires and tries to emulate.<br /> The biggest difference is of course that both can be something positive (or awful) and that the nature (at least initially) probably is something simple. They'll both most likely change during play until his journey is at its end and he's happy with himself, at which point he faces his new dawn.<br /> <br /> The aspiration could be tied to the refinements as well, considering most of them emulates different parts of humanity. Studying Mercurius the character might strive to emulate a trait of his progenitor or as a Centimani trying to be the perfect monster.<br /> The nature could be childlike traits early on and when his humanity has increased (low starting humanity seems to be a popular idea here) or he's simply lived long enough it'll change into something more mature, could probably just use the Masks/Dirges from vampire.<br /> <br /> A lot more could be done with it but what do you think about the basic idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1944-cobalus","name":"cobalus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T17:12:56-08:00","id":47136,"title":"","content":"It's certainly an idea that has been discussed. I don't know if there's a need for &quot;maturity&quot; in terms of Virtue or Vice, since you could argue Vices are simplistic and pretty low-minded. I'm working on a framework that makes Virtues and Vices a reward for certain advancements. Prometheans instead begin with a Remnant of their body/bodies' original inhabitants, and also the ability to gain Willpower by means of their Refinement. The latter is in a back-to-the-drawing-board, because I'm finding the Lineage to be a better indication of the Promethean's emotional responses. Refinements are a better source of Aspirations/Milestones.<br /> <br /> The context for this framework is that Prometheans possess only the barest sense of self at their &quot;birth&quot;, and it takes some experience and suffering to draw strength from oneself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T17:24:37-08:00","id":47140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cobalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/47110-gmc-virtue-vice#post47110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot more could be done with it but what do you think about the basic idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty good, I think.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd call them <i>Lead and Gold </i>or<i> Night and Dawn</i>, to match the symbolism and terminology of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T18:36:45-08:00","id":47179,"title":"","content":"We've been working on stuff like this. Turns out it's kind of hard to bang into place. I currently am using &quot;Beacons&quot; - things from Humanity you emulate - as a sort of secondary Aspirations . You have them, you pursue them, and when you successfully resolve them - discarding them or integrating them - your understanding of Humanity grows (which is represented by gaining a new Breaking Point, not by raising Humanity; build-a-morality sounds like tons of fun).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T08:11:02-08:00","id":47392,"title":"","content":"Yeah I like the Beacons idea and remaking Disquiet into conditions, just couldn't find anything about Virtues/Vices so thougt I'd add my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1944-cobalus","name":"cobalus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T08:28:25-08:00","id":47404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/47110-gmc-virtue-vice?p=47136#post47136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's certainly an idea that has been discussed. I don't know if there's a need for &quot;maturity&quot; in terms of Virtue or Vice, since you could argue Vices are simplistic and pretty low-minded. I'm working on a framework that makes Virtues and Vices a reward for certain advancements. Prometheans instead begin with a Remnant of their body/bodies' original inhabitants, and also the ability to gain Willpower by means of their Refinement. The latter is in a back-to-the-drawing-board, because I'm finding the Lineage to be a better indication of the Promethean's emotional responses. Refinements are a better source of Aspirations/Milestones.<br /> <br /> The context for this framework is that Prometheans possess only the barest sense of self at their &quot;birth&quot;, and it takes some experience and suffering to draw strength from oneself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realise they work fine as-is, I've just been thinking and reading a lot about converting it to the GMC and came up with this, I'll probably work more on it.<br /> <br /> And personally I really dislike Residual Memory-ish stuff, though my players always work more on the bodies former owner than the current one when creating a character so I understand where you're coming from at least. The whole proto-human thing is one of my favourite parts of the game, Vampire fills my quota for post-human concepts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1944-cobalus","name":"cobalus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T09:12:22-08:00","id":49022,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I like &quot;Lead&quot; and &quot;Gold.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T15:30:37-08:00","id":50158,"title":"","content":"Personally I think that, for the most part, until its chronicle book comes out, it's easier to simply use a small variation of GMC Mortal Virtue/Vice. Because making large changes tends to need a good amount of playtests to ensure they work as expected.<br /> <br /> For example for changeling: I'm making it almost the exact same as a mortals Virtue/Vice but at high wyrd, the Virtue acts like the Vice and Vice Versa. it's small but still works","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T16:06:59-08:00","id":50199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/47110-gmc-virtue-vice?p=50158#post50158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think that, for the most part, until its chronicle book comes out, it's easier to simply use a small variation of GMC Mortal Virtue/Vice. Because making large changes tends to need a good amount of playtests to ensure they work as expected.<br /> <br /> For example for changeling: I'm making it almost the exact same as a mortals Virtue/Vice but at high wyrd, the Virtue acts like the Vice and Vice Versa. it's small but still works</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you, I'd probably rephrase and use Masks/Dirges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1944-cobalus","name":"cobalus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T21:40:59-08:00","id":50423,"title":"","content":"This is my biggest issue, really, with changing Virtue/Vice to some kind of &quot;Anchors&quot; for Prometheans. It requires playtesting, changing other parts of the system that objectively work fine, and drives me a little batty.<br /> That, and I think everyone kind of has a different vision of what Promethean Anchors should be - but everyone can understand how the Virtue/Vice dichotomy works, and everyone can use it.<br /> <br /> I do like Lead/Gold. I like the idea that one is the Promethean's &quot;Self&quot; and the other is what &quot;weighs them down on the Pilgrimage.&quot; That would be neat and easy.<br /> I'm pitching Beacons for their &quot;goals&quot; on the Pilgrimage; I think, since they have to be of humanity, it makes sense to have a whole slew of &quot;things I want to be like when I'm human&quot; as your secondary Aspirations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T14:01:23-08:00","id":51039,"title":"","content":"Minor nitpick: as I view it, the whole point of the Pilgrimage is that the Promethean <i>doesn\u2019t</i> have a Self: it is an organic machine with behaviors that arise out of its Humour and the residual \u201cprogramming\u201d (e.g., muscle memory, language facility, etc.) of the body. That <i>lack of</i> Self is what humans instinctively sense when they meet a Promethean, and is the root cause of Disquiet. Gold and Lead aren\u2019t \u201cSelf\u201d and \u201cwhat weighs them down\u201d; they\u2019re \u201cwhat is my Pilgrimage\u2019s destination?\u201d and \u201cwhat was my Pilgrimage\u2019s origin?\u201d For those who like the notion of Purpose-built Prometheans, Lead is their original Purpose; and Gold is the \u201cSelf\u201d tat they\u2019re striving to attain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T16:10:02-08:00","id":51138,"title":"","content":"Rather than purpose - which might not be present at all in any meaningful way - Lead could be considered a minor reflection of the Promethean's creator, the way Lineages reflect the obsessions of their demiurges. Or to put it another way, Lead reflects where their maker was at when they were made. It retains the hollowness of Promethean's existence, that one of the two personality traits is about someone else. Purpose is of course a big subset of that - making a Promethean is a big undertaking, so there'll be a lot of conflation between why you're making one and where you're at in yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T17:22:14-08:00","id":51995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/47110-gmc-virtue-vice?p=49022#post49022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, I like &quot;Lead&quot; and &quot;Gold.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I demand a writer credit in the inevitable GMC update!<br /> (I do not demand a writer credit in the inevitable GMC update.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T23:31:51-08:00","id":53039,"title":"","content":"So, here are a couple of the discussions that have touched on the topic, since cobalus said he didn't find them.<ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/7219-house-ruled-promethean-gmc-patches\">House-Ruled GMC Patches</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/29145-stolen-lives\">Stolen Lives</a></li> </ul>But Lead and Gold...<br /> <br /> So, my hitch here is that they're tied to the Pilgrimage. Great! But. So is everything else about the Promethean, to the point where it can be a stubborn point of pride <i>not</i> to Pilgrimagize. If you take what is the basic game psychology of the Promethean, and make that also a part of the Great Work, then what of Man is there in the Promethean? &quot;Oh, she's a Refuser, she lets her Lead drag her down.&quot; You need a better anchor to hang it on than alchemical motifs that are already used as <i>Refinements</i>. Lead &amp; Gold does two disservices to the Promethean: first, it displaces Virtue and Vice, robbing them of possible human connections. Second, it reduces the extremes of their personality to facets of the Pilgrimage, not even allowing them the illusion of self-determination.<br /> <br /> So, come at Lead and Gold from a different angle. It needs to be different enough from existing traits to justify its own existence, else it requires a re-imagining of <i>other</i> traits. As an intended replacement of Virtue and Vice, it needs to do the job thereof, while meeting the previous stipulation, and conveying certain themes and natures of the Promethean psyche. Finally, it needs to be a matter of choice for the character, a statement of who he wishes to be (or not be), with real rewards in order spur the player's investment in that character.<br /> <br /> In my Stolen Lives setup, one of these was the Remnant, a shred of the Promethean's host body's original inhabitant. &quot;Stolen Lives&quot; is in the game's subtitle, but not a lot calls it out in the game book. That would be &quot;Lead&quot; in my take, because the Remnant is something to overcome in order to gain Mortality, but it offers such a comforting sense of identity and belonging that it's easy to fall into its trap and lose the plot of the Pilgrimage. &quot;Gold&quot; would be something else; Refinement, perhaps, since it represents the chosen &quot;true&quot; path to the New Dawn, and when the Promethean achieves a Refinement-specific Milestone, he also gains a sense of the reality of Mortality, and the correctness of his choices.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this to pimp my ideas or put down others', just trying to inject more confusion into the topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:43:44-08:00","id":53471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/47110-gmc-virtue-vice?p=51039#post51039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor nitpick: as I view it, the whole point of the Pilgrimage is that the Promethean <i>doesn\u2019t</i> have a Self: it is an organic machine with behaviors that arise out of its Humour and the residual \u201cprogramming\u201d (e.g., muscle memory, language facility, etc.) of the body. That <i>lack of</i> Self is what humans instinctively sense when they meet a Promethean, and is the root cause of Disquiet. Gold and Lead aren\u2019t \u201cSelf\u201d and \u201cwhat weighs them down\u201d; they\u2019re \u201cwhat is my Pilgrimage\u2019s destination?\u201d and \u201cwhat was my Pilgrimage\u2019s origin?\u201d For those who like the notion of Purpose-built Prometheans, Lead is their original Purpose; and Gold is the \u201cSelf\u201d tat they\u2019re striving to attain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about this for a few days, and I have to disagree.<br /> I suppose it depends on what your definition of &quot;self&quot; is, but coming at it from a psychological/sociological viewpoint:<br /> <br /> I disagree because of the existential difficulty of not having a &quot;self.&quot; People who do not have &quot;selves,&quot; as far as psychologists and sociologists are concerned, are those raised feral, by animals or by terrible vial parents. Both of these are recorded, and the poor children (I tend to think the later is the worse) in question still have rudimentary understanding of the world, but not of who they are.<br /> Granted, you need a society to interact with to forge a self, but your basic starting Promethean character is going to be much more PC-able then the real-world examples of &quot;people without a self.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Promethean condition is a lot similar to Borderline Personality Disorder than this, which is basically what it says on the tin. I think that's a more accurate way to describe a Promethean's state-of-being. It also allows characters which are playable, since you can't relate to someone without a self.<br /> Seriously, look it up with Torment, Refinements and Disquiet in mind. Very similar.<br /> If you can't relate to your own character, that's a problem. I'd hate for a game to tell me &quot;your character doesn't have a self!&quot; That basically means they have <i>nothing</i> for me to cling to.<br /> Sure, you can pitch that they're an organic machine, but I find the idea that Prometheans <i>have</i> all these important qualities that make up a person, they just have to uncover them within to become that person. They have to make choices and decide what is moral and what isn't and fall in and out of love and lead a life before they get to <i>have</i> a life: just like the person(s) they were made from.<br /> <br /> The core book is pretty clear that Prometheans still feel emotions, want things besides food and water, get bored, and are curious. Those indicate a self, to me.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I'm really not a fan of <i>any</i> of the suggested alternate Anchors (not that my opinion matters for your game, but still). They just seem, inaccurate.<br /> None of them really seem to express what makes a Promethean's core being. Verge has a lot of good ideas, and I agree that over-placing emphasis on the Pilgrimage robs the Promethean of what little tie to humanity they already have: that's actually my biggest issue with alternate Anchors.<br /> <br /> Look: Pandorans get Vices, and only Vices, while Prometheans get Virtues and Vice. The biggest difference - from an existential/philosophical viewpoint - between a Promethean and a Pandoran is the Created's Virtue and it's Azoth. Your bastard children hate you because they can never be like you, what with your proto-soul and your <i>positive qualities.</i><br /> <br /> If you need to change the names of the Promethean Anchors to Lead and Gold, ok, but how those are different from Vice and Virtue (respectively), I'm not sure. I think Refinement provides enough space that you could, as Verge has already done, write up some Willpower-resotration Conditions for them similar to Mask/Dirge. I think you could do some cool stuff with the idea of weight, still, since Weight is the Pilgrim's natural enemy: guys, you want to travel light, but the Promethean is carrying an awful lot of baggage.<br /> <br /> I dunno if you need to change Virtue and Vice, though. I still haven't been convinced it's as necessary as changing Milestones and Humanity.<br /> <br /> Tangentially, there's &quot;Simulcra&quot; as a Humanity alternate, and Verge has his own (which I will not reveal for him); this thread makes me want to make one called &quot;Self&quot; and see how that plays out, since it's much easier to frame the Pilgrimage here as &quot;here are the little bits of your Self you start with, now go make more. When you're done you get a shot at the real thing.&quot;<br /> I suppose that &quot;Self&quot; is what all the alternate Humanities have been about, though. Hrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T05:41:25-08:00","id":56060,"title":"","content":"The idea of Lead/Gold was just a thematic rewriting of Virtue/Vice akin to Mask/Dirge in Blood and Smoke. They've always been a kind of incentive to play your character a certain way, which was why I thought you should be able to change them (your concept usually solidifies after a few sessions). The point was never to tie them to other thematic or mechanical concepts as that would quickly get out of hand.<br /> <br /> I'm also with Ben Quo on the Pilgrimage. Prometheans to me are broken pre-humans with primitive feelings and a rather naive outlook on things, not occult machines (The humours are just basic guidelines to me) on a set path. They're still persons first and foremost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1944-cobalus","name":"cobalus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T16:22:35-08:00","id":56413,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s not an either/or \u2014 though I wouldn\u2019t use the term \u201cbroken\u201d so much as \u201cincomplete\u201d. As I see it, the \u201coccult machine\u201d bit is the framework that keeps the Promethean functional as it pieces together a human nature, and is most clearly seen in low-Humanity Prometheans. But even a high-Humanity Promethean is still a Promethean: a <i>simulation</i> of a real human (often a very convincing one) rather than a real human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T16:44:14-08:00","id":56422,"title":"","content":"Tangentially, &quot;Simulation of a real human&quot; is why the Unfleshed are a brilliant addition. AIs and the like are a hallmark of cyberpunk fiction, and here Promethean goes, giving us a gothic horror vantage to &quot;what does it mean to be human?&quot; and then injecting the robot right back into the question.<br /> <br /> Back to task.<br /> Incomplete is a fine term to use. Broken has it's appeal as well, though it does imply that all Prometheans can be fixed: I am a fan of having Redeemed NPCs who are terrible, awful human beings, but hey, that's how they learned a human should act.<br /> (usually to contrast the PCs, who are trying to be the bestest they can be).<br /> <br /> An idea I cooked up recently was leaving Virtue/Vice as-is, but letting the Promethean change one or the other (and only one or the other) in some noticeable manner every time they switch Refinements or Resolve a Beacon (complete a Milestone, if you're using RAW).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it's a good idea or not. It wouldn't be necessary when you meet one of those scenarios, but it would let the event-in-question have that much extra oomph: hey, I chose a new Road so I have a new Vice, the better to exemplify the new element/Hey, I got this doctor to teach me some medicine so I see new hope in Humanity and that's my new Virtue.<br /> It would simulate that the character hasn't figured himself out yet, yes, but also that he's on a journey to self-discovery, since basically each time he changes Virtue/Vice he adopts/discards a new facet of his &quot;self.&quot;<br /> <br /> My first attempt at updating Promethean was with Blood &amp; Smoke spoilers (not even the whole thing, this was back in - July?), and honestly? I ported a lot of stuff that didn't need to be ported. It has been smoothed out recently, but that's still my key question: do we need to change it? What does a re-write actually add to the game, that Virtue/Vice doesn't already do fine? Mask/Dirge makes it clear that &quot;Vampires are once-human monsters.&quot; Letting Prometheans swap out Virtue and Vice easier than anyone else, at least, lets it *feel* like a journey and a discovery of the self as your &quot;self&quot; changes and grows.<br /> <br /> Cobalus: I agree with your assessment about the hand-ed-ness of it. It's partially why I prefer to leave them as-is (the &quot;robbing of the human connection&quot; bit Verge mentioned is another factor).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T00:27:51-08:00","id":56614,"title":"","content":"Hey, that's my name!<br /> <br /> I don't see much of a problem with leaving Virtue and Vice where they are; while I tend to view them as phenomena of a &quot;matured&quot; personality, they can still be used to define certain tendencies even in children and Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Having recently purchased Blood &amp; Strix, I came to notice how dramatically Mask &amp; Dirge differ from V&amp;V. Each is its own Virtue and Vice combo, with a single and full WP criterion. I was a little disappointed that M&amp;D chose from the same pool, but it still works in that they exist independently of one another (if the Kindred knows what's good for him!). Sadly, the archetypes can't be imported directly into Promethean without heavy editing.<br /> <br /> It did get me to refine my Remnant idea some. The Remnant, being a shadow of the person(s) before the Promethean, is a cheap and easy source of self-consciousness. During character creation, the player and Storyteller hash out some details, and devolving from that conception comes a Remnant archetype and a [Humanity} 3 Breaking Point. When the character hits {Humanity} 5, and has Touchstone-analogs, none of which are connected to the Remnant's life, he or she can resolve the Remnant by means of a dramatic failure or exceptional success when testing against the Remnant's Breaking Point, thus erasing the Breaking Point, and swapping the archetype for a human Virtue or Vice.<br /> <br /> Cobalus has the right of it: they're all incentives to play characters a certain way. A key consideration for Prometheans is that their systems are already set up for that. Milestones, Torment, the pressures of Disquiet and the Wasteland: a Promethean should be paranoid, stressed-out, and desperate, almost with no time for an actual personality. Refinements suggest what they should do, and Lineages suggest how they'll react.<br /> <br /> Now that I've put it in those terms, a Promethean really ought to have a vice, or why even continue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T06:42:06-08:00","id":313641,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/first-principles-basic-refinements/\" target=\"_blank\">Hmm:</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ila hijacked a factory and constructed a body for herself. She avoids humans both because she fears them and because she is unused to independent articulation. She perseveres in the hope that someday, maybe, she can talk to her creator, and they won\u2019t be afraid of her this time.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}